  "term": "ataxic speech",
  "definition": "Ataxic speech is a type of dysarthria, meaning a speech-motor disorder pattern within a clinical classification of abnormal speech. In this context, it refers to one of the recognised speech feature clusters used to describe speech problems seen in neurological disease.",
